//@version=6
// P-12 3m LTF PARENT-ATTRIBUTED EXTRACTION PROBE -- DATA EXTRACTION ONLY.
//
// Sibling of docs/p11_3m_extraction_probe.pine, which is NOT modified: that file
// is the record of what P-11 ran. docs/p9_extraction_probe.pine likewise stays
// byte-identical.
//
// WHY THIS EXISTS
// P-11 persisted only the 3m bar timestamps, so the parent each bar was
// attributed to was lost. The eligibility audit then showed that re-deriving it
// as `timestamp - (timestamp % 300)` disagrees with TradingView on every
// straddling bar -- 40% of the stream. Attribution must therefore be OBSERVED,
// never reconstructed.
//
// HOW THE ATTRIBUTION IS OBSERVED
// request.security_lower_tf() delivers, on each 5m chart bar, exactly the array
// of lower-timeframe bars TradingView assigns to THAT parent. The parent is
// therefore the bar the study is executing on, and its timestamp is plain
// `time`. Publishing `time` as `pt` makes that relationship an explicit,
// read-back output rather than an inference. It is also independently
// recoverable as the study series' own bar time, so the two can be cross-checked
// against each other on every row.
//
// Contains no strategy logic whatsoever: no ATR, pivots, swings, sweep, CHOCH,
// BOS, displacement, FVG, entry, stop, target, risk, P&L, signals or
// performance. It requests the lower-timeframe arrays and republishes them.
indicator("P12 3M LTF PARENT-ATTRIBUTED", overlay=false)

ltfStr = input.string("3", "lower timeframe", options=["3"])

// Frozen pre-FE boundary, recovered from repository evidence, not chosen here:
//   trader_v2/V53_ltf_sequence.pine:33  FE = 1788134400000
//   bot/guards.py                       FE_MS = 1788134400000
// Convention is EXCLUSIVE, matching V53's inFold: (time < FE).
FE = 1788134400000

aO = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, ltfStr, open)
aH = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, ltfStr, high)
aL = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, ltfStr, low)
aC = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, ltfStr, close)
aT = request.security_lower_tf(syminfo.tickerid, ltfStr, time)

// Parent-level pre-FE gate: nothing is emitted for a parent at or after FE, so
// no post-FE lower-timeframe value can ever reach a plot. Pre-FE bounded at
// source -- post-FE rows are never produced and never need trimming.
preFE = time < FE

gf(arr, k) => array.size(arr) > k ? array.get(arr, k) : na
gt(k) => array.size(aT) > k ? array.get(aT, k) / 1000 : na

n = preFE ? array.size(aC) : na
plot(n, "n")

// THE ATTRIBUTION ITSELF: the parent bar this array was delivered on.
plot(preFE ? time / 1000 : na, "pt")

plot(preFE ? gt(0)     : na, "t0")
plot(preFE ? gf(aO, 0) : na, "o0")
plot(preFE ? gf(aH, 0) : na, "h0")
plot(preFE ? gf(aL, 0) : na, "l0")
plot(preFE ? gf(aC, 0) : na, "c0")

plot(preFE ? gt(1)     : na, "t1")
plot(preFE ? gf(aO, 1) : na, "o1")
plot(preFE ? gf(aH, 1) : na, "h1")
plot(preFE ? gf(aL, 1) : na, "l1")
plot(preFE ? gf(aC, 1) : na, "c1")

// Overflow/integrity detector only; never expected to be non-na at 3m under 5m.
plot(preFE ? gt(2)     : na, "t2")
plot(preFE ? gf(aO, 2) : na, "o2")
plot(preFE ? gf(aH, 2) : na, "h2")
plot(preFE ? gf(aL, 2) : na, "l2")
plot(preFE ? gf(aC, 2) : na, "c2")
